The runtime is original code. It is built with, links or can link, the following third-party components, which keep
their own licences (none of their source code is copied into this directory):

* ESP-IDF (Espressif Systems, Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf): build system, FreeRTOS port,
  heap, flash partition, memory-mapping and I2S APIs used by components/steertts_nano/port, bench/, main/ and
  the examples.
  FreeRTOS kernel (MIT License) is part of ESP-IDF.
* esp-dsp (Espressif Systems, Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/espressif/esp-dsp): its optimized radix-2 complex
  FFT kernel (dsps_fft2r_fc32) is used on the ESP32-S3 when the component is available; tools/gen_tables.py writes the
  twiddle table in esp-dsp's layout. The ESP-IDF build fetches it through the component manager
  (components/steertts_nano/idf_component.yml); Arduino-ESP32 ships it.
* esp-nn (Espressif Systems, Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/espressif/esp-nn): not linked. The int8
  requantization follows the same TFLite / gemmlowp reference arithmetic that esp-nn implements (bit-exact path), so
  results match esp-nn and TensorFlow Lite Micro kernels.
* Arduino-ESP32 (Espressif Systems, LGPL 2.1, https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32) and PlatformIO
  (Apache License 2.0): used only by the example in examples/platformio; not part of the runtime.

Text front end (front/ and front.bin, built by tools/make_front_bin.py from the edge model's native/front assets):
the rules are an independent C port of the SteerTTS edge front end; front.bin holds the same data as those assets,
re-encoded, and their notices (../native/NOTICE) apply unchanged:
* the lexicon is derived from the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (Copyright (C) 1993-2015 Carnegie Mellon University;
  BSD-style license);
* the G2P model is an int8 re-encoding of the g2p_en GRU weights (Copyright 2019 Kyubyong Park and Jongseok Kim;
  Apache License 2.0);
* the heteronym tables are derived from decisions of NLTK's averaged-perceptron tagger (Apache License 2.0); the
  tokenizer follows NLTK's TweetTokenizer expressions;
* number reading ports g2p_en's normalize_numbers (from keithito/tacotron, MIT License) and inflect's
  number_to_words logic (MIT License); cardinal / ordinal words are an independent implementation matching
  num2words' English output (no num2words code is included);
* the Unicode tables are derived from CPython's unicodedata (PSF License).

Vocoder: the runtime's vocoder (src/nano_synth.c, src/nano_dsp.c) implements the Vocos architecture (ConvNeXt backbone
+ iSTFT head; Copyright (c) 2023 Charactr Inc.; MIT License, https://github.com/gemelo-ai/vocos) in int8. No Vocos
code or weights are included.

Model weights (nano.bin, downloaded from the Hugging Face Hub, WhissleAI/steer-tts-nano) are covered by their model
card and ../LICENSE.
